Subject: Kite: publish accepted PN proof before encrypted RX policy lookup

The telemetry refactor evaluated policy before setting KDP_RX_PN. Every
encrypted MPDU then failed the security precondition and fell back to host,
even with an exact policy. Keep PN validation and proof ahead of admission.

--- a/npu_kite_secure_rx.c
+++ b/npu_kite_secure_rx.c
@@ -135,10 +135,12 @@
 		if (!accepted) {
 			dp_rx_drop(ctx, id);
 		} else {
-			int policy = dp_rx_policy(s, id);
+			int policy;
 
 			r->flags |= KDP_RX_REORDERED | (m->encrypted ? KDP_RX_PN : 0);
 			KDP_BARRIER();
+			/* PN was accepted above; publish proof before policy lookup. */
+			policy = dp_rx_policy(s, id);
 			if (policy) {
 				s->stats[r->band].rx_policy_hit++;
 				if (!tdma_tx_submit(id, r->len - r->offset,
